{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3743268","formula":"FeSe₂","hill":"FeSe2","elements":["Fe","Se"],"composition":{"Fe":1.0,"Se":2.0},"names":{"en":"Ferroselite","uk":"Фероселіт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Orthorhombic ferroselite and its isometric polymorph dzharkenite are iron selenides of general formula FeSe2 precipitated under reducing conditions in anoxic environments. They are a source of selenium in the Rocky Mountains where selenium occurrence is associated with Upper Cretaceous shale deposits. In the frame of safety assessment calculations made for deep disposal of high-level radioactive waste, ferroselite and dzharkenite are also considered in geochemical calculations as one of the mineral phases limiting the solubility of Selenium-79.","uk":"Фероселіт — мінерал групи марказиту, селенід заліза острівної будови. Фероселіт вперше знайдений 1955 року в родовищі урану Усть-Уюк, в Туві, Сибір (Е. З. Бурьянова, А. З. Комков). Назва походить від латинського ferro (залізо) і «sel» для селену."},"fame":11,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-760","atoms":24,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[4.78,0.0,0.0],[0.0,5.756,0.0],[0.0,0.0,3.581]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Fe"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":7.162,"el":"Fe"},{"x":0.0,"y":5.756,"z":0.0,"el":"Fe"},{"x":0.0,"y":5.756,"z":7.162,"el":"Fe"},{"x":4.78,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Fe"},{"x":4.78,"y":0.0,"z":7.162,"el":"Fe"},{"x":4.78,"y":5.756,"z":0.0,"el":"Fe"},{"x":4.78,"y":5.756,"z":7.162,"el":"Fe"},{"x":2.39,"y":2.878,"z":1.79,"el":"Fe"},{"x":1.019,"y":2.129,"z":0.0,"el":"Se"},{"x":1.019,"y":2.129,"z":7.162,"el":"Se"},{"x":3.76,"y":3.628,"z":0.0,"el":"Se"},{"x":3.76,"y":3.628,"z":7.162,"el":"Se"},{"x":3.409,"y":0.75,"z":1.79,"el":"Se"